{"schema": "workere-benchmark-suite/v1", "protocol": "workere-historical-relations/v1", "config": {"seed": 42, "active_dataset": "causal_timebank", "datasets": {"causal_timebank": {"name": "CausalTimeBank-standard-eci", "repo_id": "Nofing/CausalTimeBank-standard-eci-workere", "split": "train", "text_field": "text", "ann_field": "annots", "max_examples": 0, "kfold": {"enabled": true, "n_folds": 10}, "constrain_to_pair_list": false}}, "data": {"shuffle_docs": true, "shuffle_pair_list": true, "reshuffle_per_resample": true, "binary_undirected": false, "vote_to_binary": false, "binary_default": "norel", "novote_norel": true, "labels": ["causes", "causedby", "norel"]}, "experiment": {"resampling": {"enabled": true, "n_runs": 7, "tie_breaking": "norel", "distinct_fewshots": true}}}, "documents": [{"id": "wsj_0810", "idx": 151, "text": "Cie . de Navigation Mixte Chairman Marc Fournier <ei1 said> his board unanimously <ei2 rejected> as too low the $ 1.77 billion <ei3 bid> by Cie . Financiere de Paribas to <ei4 bring> its stake in Navigation Mixte to 66.7 % . At a news <ei5 conference> , Mr. Fournier <ei6 accused> Paribas of <ei7 planning> to <ei8 pay> for the <ei9 takeover> by selling parts of the company , whose interests include insurance , banking , tuna canning , sugar and orange juice . The chairman <ei10 said> his board members , including representatives of West German insurance giant Allianz AG and French banks Credit Lyonnais and Societe Generale , <ei11 hold> nearly 50 % of Navigation Mixte 's capital . Mr. Fournier <ei12 said> that as Navigation Mixte chairman , he is <ei13 prohibited> by takeover regulations from <ei14 organizing> his own defense or <ei15 doing> anything besides <ei16 managing> current company business . But sources <ei17 said> he will be <ei18 urging> his allies to <ei19 boost> their stakes in Navigation Mixte , which is being <ei20 traded> in London and is to <ei21 resume> <ei22 trading> in Paris Tuesday . At the same time , he is <ei24 expected> to <ei25 seek> legal and regulatory means of <ei26 blocking> or <ei27 delaying> Paribas 's <ei28 bid> . For the moment , the sources <ei29 said> , he has <ei30 decided> against <ei31 seeking> a white knight or <ei32 organizing> a <ei33 counterbid> for Paribas . Mr. Fournier <ei34 said> Navigation Mixte 's 1989 unconsolidated , or parent-company , profit is likely to be 4.7 billion francs ( $ 754.4 million ) , <ei36 up> from 633.8 million francs last year . That is due mostly to <ei39 payments> from Allianz for most of the 50 % stake it has <ei40 agreed> to <ei41 acquire> in Navigation Mixte 's insurance business . Mr. Fournier <ei42 said> the exceptional gain would <ei43 mean> nearly twice as high a dividend this year as last . If holders <ei46 avoid> <ei47 tendering> to Paribas , he <ei48 added> , they can <ei49 expect> strong dividends again next year . Analysts <ei51 noted> that over the past 20 years , Mr. Fournier has <ei53 built> his company through astute stock-market activity and has <ei54 warded> off at least three takeover <ei55 attempts> . This time , however , some analysts <ei56 think> he could <ei57 face> a real <ei58 battle> . \" Without some unexpected \" coup de theatre \" , I do n't <ei59 see> what will <ei60 block> the Paribas <ei61 bid> , \" <ei62 said> Philippe de Cholet , analyst at the brokerage Cholet - Dupont amp Cie . Mr. de Cholet <ei63 said> Mr. Fournier 's biggest hope was to somehow <ei64 persuade> regulatory authorities to <ei65 block> the <ei66 bid> . Paribas still needs the go-ahead from the Commission des Operations de Bourse , a government regulatory agency , but analysts <ei67 said> that is considered likely . Mr. Fournier also <ei68 noted> that Navigation Mixte <ei69 joined> Paribas 's core of shareholders when Paribas was <ei70 denationalized> in 1987 , and <ei72 said> it now <ei74 holds> just under 5 % of Paribas 's shares . Once he <ei75 realized> that Paribas 's intentions were n't friendly , he <ei76 said> , but before the <ei77 bid> was <ei78 launched> , he <ei79 sought> <ei80 approval> to <ei81 boost> his Paribas stake above 10 % . The petition is still <ei82 pending> , but Mr. Fournier <ei83 downplayed> the likelihood of his <ei84 organizing> a takeover <ei85 bid> of his own for the much-larger Paribas . One big question now is the likely role of Mr. Fournier 's allies . Mr. Fournier <ei86 said> the large institutions that hold nearly 50 % of Navigation Mixte 's capital all strongly <ei87 support> him , but some analysts <ei88 said> they are n't so sure . Allianz , for example , has <ei89 said> in official comments so far that it will <ei90 remain> neutral . Paribas is Allianz 's lead French bank . Paribas <ei91 said> Monday that it <ei93 intends> to <ei94 bid> to <ei95 boost> its stake in Navigation Mixte to 66.7 % , from the 18.7 % it already <ei96 owns> . The <ei97 purchase> of the additional 48 % stake is <ei98 expected> to <ei99 cost> more than 11 billion francs ( $ 1.77 billion ) . Paribas <ei100 says> it will <ei101 offer> 1,850 francs ( $ 296.95 ) each for Navigation Mixte shares that <ei102 enjoy> full dividend rights , and 1,800 francs each for a block of shares issued July 1 , which will <ei104 receive> only partial dividends this year . Alternatively , it is to <ei106 offer> three Paribas shares for one Navigation Mixte share . The Paribas offer values Navigation Mixte at about 23 billion francs , depending on how many of Navigation Mixte 's warrants are converted into shares during the takeover battle .", "gold": [], "lang": "eng", "mentions": ["ei1", "ei2", "ei3", "ei4", "ei5", "ei6", "ei7", "ei8", "ei9", "ei10", "ei11", "ei12", "ei13", "ei14", "ei15", "ei16", "ei17", "ei18", "ei19", "ei20", "ei21", "ei22", "ei24", "ei25", "ei26", "ei27", "ei28", "ei29", "ei30", "ei31", "ei32", "ei33", "ei34", "ei36", "ei39", "ei40", "ei41", "ei42", "ei43", "ei46", "ei47", "ei48", "ei49", "ei51", "ei53", "ei54", "ei55", "ei56", "ei57", "ei58", "ei59", "ei60", "ei61", "ei62", "ei63"